{
  "dom_id": "step-q1273",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "If $Y={a,b,c,d}$, which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{a,b},{c},{d}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{a,b},{b,c},{c,d}}$ is not a partition because the elements $b$ and $c$ appear in two subsets.\n\n- ${{a},{c},{d}}$ is not a partition because the element $b\\in Y$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{a,c},{b,c},{d}}$ is not a partition because the element $c$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{a,b},{c}}$ is not a partition because the element $d\\in Y$ does not appear in any subset.",
